From 927cce8467a65b7a6783dea18122d4f0b790e6c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:13:08 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: import GSWIP-3.0 vendor API headers

Import the GSWIP-3.0 (Gigabit Switch IP) API and register-layout
headers for the Intel/Lantiq xRX500 family switch cores, taken
verbatim from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198,
drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/switch-api/). These are the vendor's
definitions of the switch register file (gsw_reg.h, gsw30_reg_top.h,
gsw_reg_top.h), the low-level function/ops surface (gsw_ll_func.h,
gsw_flow_ops.h, adap_ops.h, mac_ops.h), the core device model
(gsw_flow_core.h, gsw_dev.h, gsw_init.h, gsw_irq.h, gsw_tbl_rw.h,
gsw_types.h) and the public ioctl-style API (lantiq_gsw.h,
lantiq_gsw_api.h, lantiq_gsw_flow.h, lantiq_gsw_routing.h,
gsw_ioctlcmd_type.h).

Licensing: the files carry Lantiq Deutschland GmbH (2012-2015) and
Intel Corporation (2016-2017) copyright banners - preserved here -
and point at the LICENSE file of the vendor "switch-api" software
module. In the AVM source drop that file declares a dual GPL /
2-clause-BSD license (Copyright (c) 2009-2015 LANTIQ
BETEILIGUNGS-GMBH & CO. KG); it was not imported into this tree, so
the pointer would dangle. Elect GPL-2.0-only (a permitted choice
under the dual license, and the terms the code was distributed
under as part of AVM's GPL kernel drop), tag every header with the
SPDX identifier, and drop the stale LICENSE-file pointer. One raw
cp1252 0x96 byte (an en-dash) in a mac_ops.h comment is replaced
with a plain '-' so the file is valid ASCII/UTF-8.

Known vendor-header warts retained for byte-faithfulness to the
working reference (to be cleaned in a follow-up once the port is
stable): gsw_types.h typedefs u8/u16/u32/u64 style scalar types
instead of using linux/types.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
